# ==============================================================================
# .gitignore - Military Transition Companion
# ==============================================================================
#
# PRIVACY STANCE:
#   Only README.md is publicly tracked.
#   All other .md files (governance, design specs, ADRs, plans, research,
#   templates, archives) are intentionally NOT tracked.
#
# RATIONALE:
#   - Solo dev: the only person who needs the design/methodology is Max
#   - Competitive intel protection: don't hand competitors the full reasoning
#   - Selective sharing: specific docs may be shared with future employers
#     by sending local copies, not by making them public via git history
#
# RESULT:
#   - Public GitHub view: README.md + code + license + standard config
#   - Local working copy: all governance, specs, ADRs, plans, research
#
# ==============================================================================

# ---- Markdown files (only README.md + docs/engineering/ tracked) ----
*.md
!README.md
!docs/engineering/**/*.md

# ---- CSV Files ----
*.csv

# ---- OS and IDE noise ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---- Node.js / PWA build artifacts ----
node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
.output/
.next/
.nuxt/
.svelte-kit/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.turbo/
.vercel/
.netlify/
.wrangler/
vite.config.js.timestamp-*
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# ---- Package manager noise ----
yarn-error.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.npm/
.yarn/
.pnpm-store/

# ---- Environment and secrets ----
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
secrets/
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# ---- Python (content-ops pipeline) ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- Test outputs ----
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov
playwright-report/
test-results/
.lighthouseci/
.vitest-cache/

# ---- Logs ----
*.log
logs/

# ---- Claude Code / superpowers session artifacts ----
.claude/
.superpowers/
.cursor/
.worktrees/

# ---- Content corpus outputs (large generated artifacts) ----
content-ops/outputs/
content-ops/review_queue/
# A2 ingest: staged source PDFs (large binaries; re-fetch from tapevents.mil - see content-ops/staged/STAGING.txt)
content-ops/staged/*.pdf
# A2 ingest: human-saved HTML for Akamai-blocked sources (see content-ops/staged/manual-html/README.txt)
content-ops/staged/manual-html/*.html
content-ops/staged/manual-html/*_files/
# A2 ingest: generated audit copies + extracted text (regeneratable via `pnpm ingest`)
content-ops/captures/
content-ops/extracted/
# A3 chunk: per-source CorpusChunk arrays (regeneratable via `pnpm chunk`)
content-ops/chunks/
# Clean: the cleaned extractions + the dated review report are regeneratable and stay untracked, but the
# approval manifest (per-source cleanedHash + decision + dropped/stripped counts) is COMMITTED as the
# corpus's provenance - its human approval decisions are judgments a fresh `pnpm clean` resets to pending,
# so they are NOT regeneratable and must live in version control alongside the corpus they gate.
content-ops/cleaned/*
!content-ops/cleaned/manifest.json
# Refresh: staging captures + the review report + pending manifest (regeneratable via `pnpm refresh`)
content-ops/refresh/

# ---- Misc local-only ----
TODO.private
NOTES.private
*.local

# ==============================================================================
# What IS tracked (visible in public repo):
#   - README.md (project introduction)
#   - LICENSE (open source license, TBD AGPL vs MIT)
#   - All source code (src/, tests/)
#   - Package config (package.json, tsconfig.json, etc.)
#   - CI config (.github/workflows/)
#   - Build config (vite.config.ts, etc.)
#   - .gitignore itself
#   - Public security policy (.well-known/security.txt - when added)
# ==============================================================================
